Revision history for Business-GoCardless

1.01     2026-10-29
        - Security fixes, reported by CPANSec automated scanning:
          - 1  CVE-2026-119036  legacy webhook flattened before its check     memory exhaustion   0.07*-1.00
          - 2  CVE-2026-119037  undef or empty secret verifies any signature  forged webhooks     0.07*-1.00
          - 3  CVE-2026-119038  redirect flow not bound to the caller         charges another's   0.17*-1.00

1.00     2026-10-19
        - MAJOR UPDATE including some breaking changes, see below
        - Add company_name, phone_number, and danish_identity_number
          attributes to Business::GoCardless::Customer
        - Add faster_ach and scheme attributes to Business::GoCardless::Payment
        - Fix typo in Payment->withdrawn (customer_appoval_denied ->
          customer_approval_denied)
        - Add bounced status check to Business::GoCardless::Payout
        - Add mandate_reference attribute to Business::GoCardless::RedirectFlow
        - Add count, app_fee, retry_if_possible,
          earliest_charge_date_after_resume, and parent_plan_paused
          attributes to Business::GoCardless::Subscription
        - Add pending_customer_approval, customer_approval_denied, finished,
          and paused status checks to Business::GoCardless::Subscription
        - Fix Pro->customer( $id ), which returned an unpopulated object due
          to using the wrong response key
        - Fix pagination in the Pro (v2) API: the Paginator now uses the
          cursors in the response meta data, previously only the first page
          of results was ever returned
        - Payment->refund now creates a refund via the /refunds endpoint and
          returns a new Business::GoCardless::Refund object (it previously
          always returned 0). The amount to refund must be passed explicitly
        - Mandate->update now returns the updated Mandate object rather than
          the raw response data (BREAKING CHANGE if you used the return value)
        - Webhook::Event->resources now supports refunds and customers events,
          add is_customer method
        - Webhook::V2 objects from Pro->webhooks now have the webhook delivery
          attributes (id, url, response_code, successful, is_test, etc)
        - Decode API responses as UTF-8, previously strings containing non
          ASCII characters were returned as UTF-8 encoded bytes rather than
          characters (BREAKING CHANGE if you were decoding them yourself).
          Webhook::V2 now also decodes the webhook body as UTF-8
        - Fix Pro->confirm_resource for redirect flows backed by a billing
          request (the default for redirect flows now), these are completed
          by GoCardless when the customer finishes the flow so trying to
          complete them again caused an error
        - Fix Pro->confirm_resource passing all of the redirect flow's links
          when creating the payment / subscription, which is now rejected by
          the API as only the mandate link is permitted
        - Update t/004_end_to_end_pro.t to work with the current GoCardless
          sandbox, it now plays the part of the customer through the billing
          requests API rather than scraping the (now javascript) payment pages
        - Remove t/gocardless_callback_reader.pl and t/end_to_end/ as they are
          no longer needed by the end to end test, and the LWP::Simple and
          FindBin build requirements that were only used by that test
        - Pro (v2) API requests that create a resource are now sent with an
          Idempotency-Key header (a UUID v4, or pass your own as a header to
          the api_post method). If an idempotent_creation_conflict error is
          returned the existing resource is fetched and returned, unless the
          new raise_on_idempotency_conflict client attribute is set. Adds a
          dependency on UUID (0.34+) for generating the keys
        - Pro (v2) API requests are now retried on network errors, server
          errors (500, 502, 503, 504), and when rate limited (429), if it is
          safe to do so. See the new max_retries (default 3) and
          max_retry_wait (default 60s) client attributes, set max_retries to
          0 for the previous behaviour
        - Add rate_limit client attribute, containing the details from the
          ratelimit-* headers of the most recent response
        - Add api_delete method to Business::GoCardless::Client, and allow
          passing extra headers to all of the api_* methods
        - Business::GoCardless::Exception now has the details of Pro (v2) API
          errors: type, request_id, documentation_url, and errors attributes,
          and reasons, has_reason, and conflicting_resource_id methods
        - webhook_secret can now be an arrayref of secrets, allowing for the
          rotation of webhook secrets
        - Add support for the rest of the Pro (v2) API resources, see the
          RESOURCE METHODS section of Business::GoCardless::Pro:
            - Billing Requests, Billing Request Flows, Billing Request
              Templates, Bank Authorisations, Institutions (Billing Requests
              replace Redirect Flows for new integrations)
            - Customer Bank Accounts, Customer Notifications, Bank Account
              Details, Bank Details Lookups, Events
            - Creditors, Creditor Bank Accounts, Verification Details
            - Refunds, Instalment Schedules, Tax Rates
            - Mandate Imports, Mandate Import Entries, Mandate PDFs,
              Transferred Mandates
            - Payout Items, Balances, Funds Availability, Negative Balance
              Limits, Currency Exchange Rates
            - Blocks, Logos, Payer Themes, Scheme Identifiers, Exports
            - Outbound Payments, Outbound Payment Imports, Outbound Payment
              Import Entries, Bank Account Holder Verifications, Payment
              Accounts, Payment Account Transactions
            - Scenario Simulators (sandbox only)
        - Add the missing operations on existing resources: create, update,
          and remove customers; list and create mandates, reinstate mandate;
          create and update subscriptions, pause and resume subscription;
          update payments, payouts, and refunds; retry webhooks; cancel and
          retry payments with metadata
        - All of the create_* methods take an idempotency_key param
        - Webhook::Event objects now have the metadata, resource_metadata,
          customer_notifications, and source attributes, and ->resources
          supports more resource types
        - Fix Business::GoCardless->payouts( %filters ) with the Pro (v2)
          API, which passed the filters incorrectly
        - Payer Authorisations are not supported as they are deprecated in
          favour of Billing Requests
        - Move github repo to payprop org
          (https://github.com/payprop/business-gocardless)
        - Update author email address to lee@payprop.com

0.45     2026-06-15
        - Add mandate_type to Business::GoCardless::Mandate, with
          is_bank_debit, is_instant, is_recurring, is_vrp_commercial,
          and is_vrp_sweeping helper methods
        - Add authorisation_source and next_possible_standard_ach_charge_date
          attributes to Business::GoCardless::Mandate
        - Add consumed, blocked, and suspended_by_payer status check methods
          to Business::GoCardless::Mandate

